WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:04.607
Hello, everyone! I'm Mr. Daniel. Welcome to Online Upper-Intermediate.

2
00:00:04.907 --> 00:00:07.992
Hi! I'm Nita. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:08.292 --> 00:00:14.915
Unit eighteen: Breakthroughs. In this unit, you will talk about science, research and plans that changed.

4
00:00:15.917 --> 00:00:17.417
laboratory research.

5
00:00:18.117 --> 00:00:21.800
laboratory research means scientific work done in a lab.

6
00:00:22.100 --> 00:00:25.040
Years of laboratory research led to the new medicine.

7
00:00:25.740 --> 00:00:28.532
Your turn. Say: laboratory research.

8
00:00:31.232 --> 00:00:32.836
laboratory research.

9
00:00:33.850 --> 00:00:34.990
clinical trial.

10
00:00:35.690 --> 00:00:39.072
clinical trial means a test of a new medicine on volunteers.

11
00:00:39.372 --> 00:00:42.021
The vaccine passed its final clinical trial.

12
00:00:42.721 --> 00:00:45.049
Your turn. Say: clinical trial.

13
00:00:47.749 --> 00:00:48.947
clinical trial.

14
00:00:49.950 --> 00:00:50.986
space mission.

15
00:00:51.686 --> 00:00:54.568
space mission means a planned journey into space.

16
00:00:54.868 --> 00:00:56.891
The space mission landed on the Moon.

17
00:00:57.591 --> 00:00:59.906
Your turn. Say: space mission.

18
00:01:02.606 --> 00:01:03.840
space mission.

19
00:01:04.850 --> 00:01:06.141
telescope image.

20
00:01:06.841 --> 00:01:10.455
telescope image means a picture of space taken by a telescope.

21
00:01:10.755 --> 00:01:13.880
The new telescope image shows a distant galaxy.

22
00:01:14.580 --> 00:01:17.244
Your turn. Say: telescope image.

23
00:01:19.944 --> 00:01:21.329
telescope image.

24
00:01:22.317 --> 00:01:23.492
quantum computing.

25
00:01:24.192 --> 00:01:27.712
quantum computing means a new, extremely powerful type of computing.

26
00:01:28.012 --> 00:01:30.650
Quantum computing could solve problems in seconds.

27
00:01:31.350 --> 00:01:34.061
Your turn. Say: quantum computing.

28
00:01:36.761 --> 00:01:38.075
quantum computing.

29
00:01:39.083 --> 00:01:40.340
nanotechnology.

30
00:01:41.040 --> 00:01:45.605
nanotechnology means technology using extremely tiny materials.

31
00:01:45.905 --> 00:01:48.984
Nanotechnology is used in sunscreen and medicine.

32
00:01:49.684 --> 00:01:52.418
Your turn. Say: nanotechnology.

33
00:01:55.118 --> 00:01:56.688
nanotechnology.

34
00:01:57.683 --> 00:01:59.079
renewable battery.

35
00:01:59.779 --> 00:02:03.822
renewable battery means a battery made from sustainable materials.

36
00:02:04.122 --> 00:02:07.155
Scientists developed a renewable battery from seaweed.

37
00:02:07.855 --> 00:02:10.565
Your turn. Say: renewable battery.

38
00:02:13.265 --> 00:02:14.696
renewable battery.

39
00:02:15.683 --> 00:02:16.951
scientific method.

40
00:02:17.651 --> 00:02:21.660
scientific method means testing ideas through observation and experiments.

41
00:02:21.960 --> 00:02:24.656
The scientific method starts with a question.

42
00:02:25.356 --> 00:02:27.892
Your turn. Say: scientific method.

43
00:02:30.592 --> 00:02:32.023
scientific method.

44
00:02:33.017 --> 00:02:34.970
Now let's listen to a conversation.

45
00:02:35.270 --> 00:02:38.221
I read that the space mission was going to launch last month.

46
00:02:39.517 --> 00:02:42.782
Yes, but it was delayed because of a technical problem.

47
00:02:44.083 --> 00:02:47.244
Scientists were about to announce a new battery too, weren't they?

48
00:02:48.550 --> 00:02:53.188
Right. They were going to publish the results, but the clinical trial took longer.

49
00:02:54.483 --> 00:02:58.143
That's the scientific method: you can't rush good research.

50
00:02:59.450 --> 00:03:04.482
Exactly. I was going to study chemistry, but now I'm thinking about physics!

51
00:03:05.783 --> 00:03:08.329
Grammar focus: Future in the past.

52
00:03:08.629 --> 00:03:12.811
Use the future in the past to talk about plans or predictions made in the past.

53
00:03:13.111 --> 00:03:15.203
Was going to, would, and was about to.

54
00:03:15.503 --> 00:03:18.072
For example: I was going to call you, but I forgot.

55
00:03:18.372 --> 00:03:21.114
Was going to often suggests that the plan did not happen.

56
00:03:22.117 --> 00:03:25.489
Now read and listen. Science Doesn't Always Go to Plan.

57
00:03:25.789 --> 00:03:29.216
The famous telescope was going to launch in 2007.

58
00:03:30.517 --> 00:03:34.374
Engineers knew it would be the most powerful telescope ever built.

59
00:03:35.683 --> 00:03:38.832
However, problems delayed the space mission for many years.

60
00:03:40.117 --> 00:03:45.588
When it finally launched in 2021, its first telescope image amazed the world.

61
00:03:46.883 --> 00:03:50.160
The story shows that patience is part of the scientific method.

62
00:03:51.450 --> 00:03:53.835
Quiz time! Choose the correct answer.

63
00:03:54.135 --> 00:03:57.006
A test of a new medicine on volunteers is a blank.

64
00:03:57.306 --> 00:04:02.039
A, clinical trial. B, space mission. C, nanotechnology.

65
00:04:06.050 --> 00:04:08.549
The answer is A: clinical trial.

66
00:04:10.050 --> 00:04:12.293
I blank visit you, but my car broke down.

67
00:04:12.593 --> 00:04:16.177
A, will. B, was going to. C, am going to.

68
00:04:20.183 --> 00:04:22.229
The answer is B: was going to.

69
00:04:23.717 --> 00:04:25.670
We were blank leave when the phone rang.

70
00:04:25.970 --> 00:04:29.287
A, about to. B, going. C, would.

71
00:04:33.283 --> 00:04:35.086
The answer is A: about to.

72
00:04:36.583 --> 00:04:40.092
Technology using extremely tiny materials is blank.

73
00:04:40.392 --> 00:04:44.754
A, quantum computing. B, nanotechnology. C, renewable battery.

74
00:04:48.750 --> 00:04:51.249
The answer is B: nanotechnology.

75
00:04:52.750 --> 00:04:56.503
According to the text, when did the telescope finally launch?

76
00:04:56.803 --> 00:05:01.756
A, 2007. B, 2015. C, 2021.

77
00:05:05.750 --> 00:05:08.736
The answer is C: 2021.

78
00:05:10.250 --> 00:05:13.750
Now it's your turn to speak. Talk about a plan you had that changed.

79
00:05:19.050 --> 00:05:25.241
I was going to study medicine, but after an internship I realised I would be happier in engineering.

80
00:05:25.541 --> 00:05:26.936
Excellent answer, Nita!

81
00:05:27.950 --> 00:05:31.427
Great work today! You learned eight new words and future in the past.

82
00:05:31.727 --> 00:05:35.552
Today's value is curiosity. Ask questions and find out.

83
00:05:35.852 --> 00:05:38.388
See you in Unit nineteen. Goodbye!

84
00:05:38.688 --> 00:05:41.433
Thank you, Mr. Daniel! Bye, everyone!

